# Fix wave 2026-09-12, review finding F4: `docker/Dockerfile`'s `COPY . .`
# had no `.dockerignore` at all, so `.env` (real secrets on a dev
# machine) and `.git` (full history) were baked into every image layer
# pushed to ECR. Everything below is either a secret, a huge/irrelevant
# local artifact, or this repo's own unrelated tooling -- none of it is
# needed to run or test Portolan inside the container.

# Secrets. Never let these into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local dev state and caches.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store

# Local file-store stand-in for S3, and anything the pipeline/bench write
# locally -- container-local by construction, and can be large.
var/
corpus/out-large/

# This repo's own memory/agent tooling and narrative context -- not part
# of the Portolan product, and none of it belongs in a shipped image.
.remember/
00-context/
02-reference-implementation/
03-talos-agent-kit/

# Bug hunt 2026-09-18 (ops review, P2 finding 11): agent worktrees
# (`.claude/`, currently 17 full repo copies locally -- Railway builds
# from GitHub so these are never in play there, but any local `docker
# build`/`railway up` would bake them in), the AWS CDK app (never
# imported by anything under portolan/ -- verified by grep), and the dev
# scripts directory (bench/eval/training scripts run with `uv run` from a
# checkout) are dev-only. The web and worker roles never read scripts/;
# `portolan.training.label_judge.judge_model_allowed` loads
# scripts/data/build_training_set.py by path, so the bench and training
# CLIs that call it do not work inside the image, and tests that need it
# skip there (`tests/_paths.py`).
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded here, despite the same finding's blanket
# suggestion: `01-spec/` and `04-brand/`. Both are read at runtime, not
# just at dev time -- `01-spec/how-portolan-works.html` is served by
# `portolan/web/routes/how_it_works.py` (`/how-it-works`, fix wave
# 2026-09-13 review finding 6, whose own docstring documents "01-spec/ is
# not excluded by .dockerignore" as a deliberate choice), and
# `04-brand/brand-tokens.css` is required by `portolan.web.templating.
# build_templates()`, which refuses to start the app at all if it's
# missing (review finding 21, `tests/test_web.py::
# test_build_templates_raises_when_brand_tokens_css_is_missing_or_empty`).
# Excluding either would build an image that 404s the explainer page or
# refuses to boot -- reproduced locally before making this change; see
# `01-spec/reviews/bughunt-2026-09-18-ops.md`'s "Fix status" table.
.claude/
infra/
scripts/

# Version control and CI config -- irrelevant inside the built image.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
